{"url": "https://lgcollege.ac.in/data/department/botany.php", "retrieved": "2026-10-02", "status": "ok", "final_url": "https://lgcollege.ac.in/data/department/botany.php", "text": "Lakhimpur Girls' College\nNAAC Reports\nE-Journal KANCHIOLI\nContact Us\nHOME\nAISHE Data\nLakhimpur Girls' College\nAffiliated to Dibrugarh University\nReaccredited by NAAC with Grade B++ (CGPA 2.91)\nAbout\nAbout the College\nVision & Mission\nCollege Anthem\nCollege Campus\nHow to reach\nAnnual Reports\nAudit Reports\nMaintenance Policies\nConstitution of Students' Union\nAction Plan: 2017-2022\nInstitutional Development Plan\nAdministration\nGoverning Body\nPrincipal's Office\nTeaching Staff\nNon-Teaching Staff\nOrganogram\nDifferent Committees\nAnti Ragging Committee\nInternal Complaints Committee\nHandbook of Code of Conduct\nAcademics\nDepartments\nProgrammes & Courses\nAdd-on Courses\nDistance Education\nCourse Structure/Syllabus\nAcademic Calendar\nTime Table/Teaching Plan\nAdmission\nAdmission Procedure\nProspectus\nAdmission Notifications\nApplication for Admission\nStudents' Corner\nGeneral Rules & Discipline\nStudents' Code of Conduct\nScholarship Schemes\nStudents' Union\nGrievance Redressal Cell\nCareer Counselling Cell\nStudents' Portal\nNational Cadet Corps (NCC)\nNational Service Scheme (NSS)\nFacilities\nLibrary\nHostel\nSports\nComputer Center\nDigital/ Smart Classrooms\nGymnasium\nCanteen\nLaboratories\nConference Hall\nCommon Room\nClassrooms\nOther Facilities\nSafety and Security\nNAAC/IQAC\nAbout IQAC\nIQAC Minutes\nAQAR List\nInstitutional Best Practices\nProgramme & Course Outcomes\nStudents' Satisfaction Survey (SSS)\nFeedback Reports\nOur Distinctiveness\nNAAC Reports\nResearch & Publication\nResearch Projects\nUndergraduate Projects\nPublication in Journals\nBook & Chapter Publication\nCollege Journal\nSeminars & Workshops\nResearch Initiatives\nExtension & Collaboration\nExtension & Outreach Programmes\nCollaboration & Linkages\nFunctional MoUs\nNIRF\nNIRF 2018\nNIRF 2019\nNIRF 2020\nNIRF 2021\nNIRF 2022\nNIRF 2023\nNIRF 2024\nDepartment of Botany\nHome\nAcademics\nDepartments\nBotany\nAnthropology\nAssamese\nBotany\nChemistry\nComputer Science\nEconomics\nEducation\nEnglish\nGeography\nHindi\nHistory\nHome Science\nMathematics\nPhilosophy\nPhysics\nPolitical Science\nZoology\nThe Department of Botany was established in 1990. This department offers higher secondary and degree courses as per the prescribed syllabus of AHSEC and Dibrugarh University respectively. To its credit, the department is actively involved in environmental issues like impact of Lower Subansiri Dam, and subsequent bio-diversity issues. The core areas of research of this department are Orchid Diversity and Macrophyte Diversity in Lakhimpur District.\nVISION\nA holistic development and academic excellence to contribute effectively to the understanding of the subject.\nTo develop an aptitude towards science and nature.\nMISSION\nTo incite students of Botany towards the immense diversity of the place and further it encompass the diversity of the entire diversity of the North-East.North-East is unique in the aspects that such type of vegetation is rare in this high altitude.\nTo train botanist to motivate masses towards the conservation of our floral and faunal diversity.\nTo train students to find and sustainably use the various biological treasures of this place.\nTo seek out uses of plants from ethnic groups and conserve them.\nTo make the students aware of the prospects of Eco-tourism.\nPROGRAMME & COURSES OFFERED\nB.Sc. in Botany (Core/ Major/ Honours)\nTo view the Programme, Programme Specific and Course Outcomes,\nClick Here\nFaculty Members:\nName\nDesignation\nQualification\nDate of Joining\nProfile\nMr Jyoti Prasad Borah\nAssociate Professor\nMSc\n1994-11-28\nView Profile\nMs Malabika Chaliha\nAssociate Professor (HOD)\nMSc in Botany\n1998-03-03\nView Profile\nMs Jyoti Rekha Saikia\nAssistant Professor\nMSc, BEd, MPhil\n2002-07-17\nView Profile